  39:     """
  40:     Slide each right-edge colored run left within its row until it is packed against the nearest fixed barrier or the left edge.
  41: 
  42:     Input structure
  43:     - The background is the dominant color.
  44:     - There are exactly two foreground colors: fixed barrier pixels and moving pixels.
  45:     - In every row where the moving color appears, it forms one contiguous horizontal run ending at the right edge.
  46: 
  47:     Rule
  48:     - Process each occupied row independently.
  49:     - Clear the moving run from the right edge.
  50:     - Repaint that run starting immediately to the right of the row's rightmost barrier pixel, or at column 0 when no barrier is present.
  51:     - Keep the barrier pixels and all rows without moving pixels unchanged.
  52: 
  53:     Key insight
  54:     - The fixed pixels are row-wise stoppers; each moving run simply slides left as far as possible without crossing the nearest stopper.
  55:     """
